        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4re7h7t",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Goods and Services Tax (GST)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2ndynkq",
      "content": "• Introduced on 1 July 2017"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "b9c564z",
      "content": "• Replaced many indirect taxes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vc5l6fc",
      "content": "• Known as 'One Nation One Tax' reform"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "722bx5x",
      "content": "• Types: CGST, SGST and IGST"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The word 'Budget' is nowhere mentioned in the Constitution of India.",
        "Fiscal Deficit = Total Expenditure - Total Receipts (excluding borrowings).",
        "Primary Deficit = Fiscal Deficit - Interest Payments.",
        "GST is a comprehensive, multi-stage, destination-based tax levied on every value addition."
      ],
      "id": "jvp2738"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3ayopg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Budget Deficit"
    },
    {
      "id": "2p1e832",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Deficit Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Fiscal Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Total expenditure minus total revenue</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Revenue Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Revenue expenditure minus revenue receipts</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Primary Deficit</p>",
            "<p>Fiscal deficit minus interest payments</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tv43iwd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fcyn7p4",
      "content": "• Union Budget is presented by the Finance Minister."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yza8zeu",
      "content": "• Financial year in India is April to March."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f7tskj1",
      "content": "• GST was implemented in India in 2017."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vnisd2y",
      "content": "• Article 112 of the Constitution deals with the Union Budget."
    }
  ],
